# AI output

`--ai` (or `MYDIFF_AI=1`, or `-f ai`) prints compact annotated text for
coding agents and LLM prompts: a summary first, then every line with both
line numbers and its exact text. It never opens the viewer.

```console
$ mydiff --ai a.txt b.txt
? 1
mydiff-ai v1
compare: a.txt -> b.txt
summary: text, +2 -1 lines in 1 hunk
@@ #1 -1,3 +1,4 @@
1 1   one
2   - two
  2 + 2
3 3   three
  4 + four

$ mydiff --ai a.txt a.txt
mydiff-ai v1
compare: a.txt -> a.txt
summary: identical

```

Folders list every changed file first. Lockfiles and minified files are listed
but not expanded until `--include` names them.

```console
$ mydiff --ai left right
? 1
mydiff-ai v1
compare: left -> right
summary: 4 files changed: 2 modified, 1 added, 1 deleted; +5 -3 lines
files:
  M Cargo.lock +1 -1 (lockfile; collapsed)
  A docs/guide.md +1
  D gone.txt -1
  M src/main.rs +3 -1

=== A docs/guide.md
@@ docs/guide.md#1 -0,0 +1,1 @@
  1 + # Guide

=== D gone.txt
@@ gone.txt#1 -1,1 +0,0 @@
1   - old

=== M src/main.rs
@@ src/main.rs#1 -1,1 +1,3 @@
1   - fn main() {}
  1 + fn main() {
  2 +     run();
  3 + }

$ mydiff --ai --include Cargo.lock left right
? 1
mydiff-ai v1
compare: left -> right
summary: 1 file changed: 1 modified; +1 -1 lines
files:
  M Cargo.lock +1 -1

=== M Cargo.lock
@@ Cargo.lock#1 -1,1 +1,1 @@
1   - v = 1
  1 + v = 2

```

Output stops at a line budget (`--budget`, `MYDIFF_AI_BUDGET`, default 2000)
and says what it left out. `--hunk <id>` shows just those hunks, in full;
`--budget` and `--hunk` imply `--ai`.

```console
$ mydiff --budget 14 long_a.txt long_b.txt
? 1
mydiff-ai v1
compare: long_a.txt -> long_b.txt
summary: text, +3 -3 lines in 3 hunks
@@ #1 -2,7 +2,7 @@
2 2   line 2
3 3   line 3
4 4   line 4
5   - line 5
  5 + LINE 5
6 6   line 6
7 7   line 7
8 8   line 8

truncated: 14-line budget reached; not shown: #2 to #3
more: rerun with --hunk #2, or --budget 0 for everything

$ mydiff --hunk 2 --hunk 9 long_a.txt long_b.txt
? 1
mydiff-ai v1
compare: long_a.txt -> long_b.txt
summary: text, +3 -3 lines in 3 hunks
@@ #2 -17,7 +17,7 @@
17 17   line 17
18 18   line 18
19 19   line 19
20    - line 20
   20 + LINE 20
21 21   line 21
22 22   line 22
23 23   line 23
not found: --hunk 9

```

JSON, YAML and CSV are compared by path.

```console
$ mydiff --ai a.json b.json
? 1
mydiff-ai v1
compare: a.json -> b.json
summary: json, 1 added, 0 removed, 1 changed
~ $.port: 80 → 8080
+ $.tls: true

```

`--ai-help` prints the format, for an agent's instructions.

```console
$ mydiff --ai-help
mydiff AI output (`mydiff --ai A B`, or set MYDIFF_AI=1)

Read-only, never interactive, no color. Exit status: 0 identical, 1 different, 2 error.
Works for files, folders and git: `mydiff --ai git show [<commit>]`,
`mydiff --ai git diff [--staged] [<rev>...]`.

Layout:
  mydiff-ai v1                      format version
  compare: <left> -> <right>
  summary: <what changed, in counts>
  files:                            (folders and git only)
    <S> <path> [+added -removed] [(tags)]
  === <S> <path>                    one section per file with content to show
  @@ <id> -<start>,<count> +<start>,<count> @@
  <left no> <right no> <marker> <text>

S (file status): M modified, A added, D deleted, R renamed (`old -> new`),
  T file vs directory, B binary, ? unreadable.
marker: ' ' unchanged, '-' left only, '+' right only, '.' ignored by options.
  A changed line is a '-' line followed by a '+' line. Text is exact.
Tags: (whitespace only), (content unchanged), (lockfile|minified; collapsed).
<id> is <path>#<n> (just #<n> for two files); pass it to --hunk.

Budget: output stops after MYDIFF_AI_BUDGET lines (default 2000) and ends
with a `truncated:` line naming what was left out. To see more, rerun with
  --hunk <id>        those hunks only, in full (repeatable)
  --include <path>   only matching files; collapsed files are then expanded
  --budget <n>       another limit; 0 = no limit
Comparison options work too: -w (ignore whitespace), -U <n> (context lines).

```
